Transformer Inference Tool

DESCRIPTION:
This tool performs transformer-based inference on Electronic Health Records (EHR) 
and laboratory test data to predict clinical outcomes and risk assessments.

FUNCTIONALITY:
- Multi-modal data processing (text + numerical)
- EHR text encoding using transformer architecture
- Lab test numerical feature extraction and normalization
- Cross-modal attention for feature fusion
- Risk score prediction and categorization

INPUT FORMAT:
1. ehr_data: List of EHR text records
   - Each entry should be a string containing clinical notes
   - Example: ["Patient presents with fatigue", "History of diabetes"]

2. lab_tests: 2D array of lab test values
   - Rows represent time points or samples
   - Columns represent different lab test types
   - Example: [[100, 20, 30], [105, 22, 31]]

OUTPUT FORMAT:
{
    "prediction_score": 0.75,       # Risk score 0-1
    "risk_category": "MODERATE",    # LOW/MODERATE/HIGH
    "confidence": 0.85,             # Model confidence
    "probabilities": {...}          # Per-class probabilities
}

USAGE NOTES:
- Ensure lab test values are normalized if comparing across different scales
- More EHR records generally improve prediction accuracy
- The model works best with standardized medical terminology

